{
  "_why": "A fake rack PC for io_facts' passive sources, built by io_facts.skeleton.fake_root. Paths in 'devices' are under sys/devices; bus and class links are derived the way the kernel makes them. Real-machine shapes (bam-GPU, 2026-10-22) for USB/xHCI/D405/C920e/fdcanusb; invented hardware is marked in '_invented'.",
  "_invented": {
    "0000:01:00.0": "Teledyne DALSA (pci vendor 11ec, Coreco Inc) frame grabber like the Xtium-CL MX4 in Zach's hyperspectral notes (Sapera config); pci.ids 2024.03.31 lists no Xtium, so device id 0x1000 and class 0x048000 are placeholders. No driver bound (Sapera not loaded).",
    "0000:08:00.0": "Magewell Pro Capture Endpoint (1cd7:0010, in pci.ids) with a V4L2 driver, trained at x1 of x4.",
    "0000:06:00.0 / 0000:07:00.0": "two Intel I210 NICs: enp6s0 driven by an IgH master (MAC in ec_master main_devices), enp7s0 by a pysoem process (EtherType 0x88A4 packet socket).",
    "1-4": "FTDI FT232R USB-serial adapter (ttyUSB0).",
    "7-2": "Realtek RTL8153 USB NIC, link down.",
    "pnp0/00:05": "a real motherboard COM port (ttyS1, 16550A)."
  },
